  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Vedettes Îles d'Or & Le Corsaire link Le Lavandou (year-round) as well as Cavalaire-sur-Mer and La Croix-Valmer (in season) to Port-Cros, Porquerolles and Le Levant. It's the most practical option if you're based on this part of the Var coast rather than near Hyères.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the company's FAQ, leashed dogs are accepted free of charge on board, except on the Seascope (glass-bottom boat, too cramped), the Caps Sauvages cruise and the Naturalist Outing (too long at sea). On the islands, the company says dogs are allowed on Porquerolles and Le Levant except on the beaches, but prohibited on <strong>Port-Cros</strong> except in the village and on the path leading to the dam (islands map on its website). Also check the National Park's regulations before departure.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: for walking with your dog, Porquerolles offers far more freedom than Port-Cros; avoid themed excursions that exclude dogs.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Le Lavandou and its long beach make a good stop before or after the crossing.</p>
